# Rules: MCP (Model Context Protocol) tool server

## PROJECT FACTS (edit these)
- Language: TypeScript (Node 20+) | Python 3.11+
- SDK: @modelcontextprotocol/sdk | mcp (python)
- Transport: stdio (default) | streamable HTTP
- Test: `npm test` | `pytest -q`
- Lint: `npm run lint` | `ruff check .`
- Entry point: src/index.ts | server.py

## Must pass before done
- Run the test and lint commands above. Both must pass.
- Run `npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector` (or the python equivalent) and confirm that tools/list returns every tool.

## Tool design
- Each tool has one job. Name tools verb_noun in snake_case (e.g. search_issues).
- Every tool has a description of 1-2 sentences that says WHEN to use it, not just what it does.
- Every input property has a type and a description. Mark required fields in `required`.
- Use enums instead of free-text strings when the value set is known.
- Return structured, compact results. Truncate long outputs and say that they were truncated.
- Errors are returned as tool results with isError: true and a message the model can act on. Do not throw raw stack traces.

## stdio safety
- NEVER write to stdout except protocol messages. Send logs to stderr.
- No interactive prompts. The server runs headless.

## Security
- Read secrets from environment variables only. Never log them. Never return them in tool output.
- Validate and bound every input (path traversal, max lengths, allowed hosts).
- Destructive tools (delete, write, send) must say so in the description and need an explicit confirm-style argument.

## Boundaries
- Do not edit generated files or the lockfile by hand.
- Do not add a dependency for something under 30 lines of code.

## Definition of done
- New or changed tool has a test that calls it through the server, not just the handler.
- README tool table updated when a tool is added, renamed or removed.
